---
args: {"hearing": "ExceptionHearing", "register": "WaiverRegister | null"}
returns: "ExceptionHearingResult"
---
1. Bind prior = register when supplied, otherwise an empty WaiverRegister at revision zero with empty pending, granted, caseAliases, policyTrials, revocationEvents and notificationReceipts. Bind identity = linkResubmittedRequests(hearing, prior). Reworded rejected requests retain case identity, but new facts must be examined rather than assumed unchanged.
2. Bind boundaries = recoverAuthorizedWaivers(hearing.caseHistory, hearing.currentRules). Preserve the actual waived requirement separately from prerequisites and surviving controls. Missing expiry is a governance defect, not perpetual permission.
3. For each current request bind analogies = retrieveRationaleContrasts(request, boundaries, hearing). Include relevant rejected and expired precedents. Bind argument = hearLimitingFacts(request, analogies, boundaries, hearing). A similar successful request is only a candidate rationale; it grants no authority. Collect the actual argument results by caseKey as currentArguments.
4. Bind currentArguments = recheckPendingPolicy(currentArguments, prior, hearing). Any governing policy change invalidates pending signing applicability and returns the affected case for re-evaluation. Preserve already valid historical actions under their actual policy and effective dates.
5. Initialize policyTrial: PolicyBoundaryTrial|null = null. Only if the supplied independent case history supports a recurring boundary problem, bind policyTrial = examinePolicyBoundaryPattern(currentArguments, boundaries, hearing). Do not turn request frequency or copied incidents into a policy rule.
6. Bind nextRegister: WaiverRegister = { revision: advance only when request identity, pending argument, or tested policy-trial state changed; otherwise preserve prior.revision, pending: replace only the affected caseKey's pending argument with its currentArguments version and preserve other pending cases, granted: prior.granted unchanged because this hearing has no matching signature receipt, caseAliases: merge identity's request IDs and fact changes by caseKey without erasing prior lineage, policyTrials: append policyTrial only when the conditional trial was actually tested and preserve earlier trials, revocationEvents: prior.revocationEvents unchanged because no revocation event was supplied, notificationReceipts: prior.notificationReceipts unchanged because no delivery receipt was supplied }. Return { register: nextRegister, arguments: currentArguments, reviewerQuestions: decisive unknown-condition questions plus governance defects and any policy-owner question actually returned by policyTrial, policyTrial, sourceRestrictions: only authorized opaque markers }. A recommendation never becomes a signed waiver without an actual matching signature receipt.
